# Textbook Review Guidance

When changing textbook answers, solution refs, crop sync, or the review tables
and RPCs (`textbook_review_*`), first read `docs/architecture/textbook-review.md`.

- Human corrections (`answer_source = 'manual'`, solution refs with `edited_at`)
  must survive machine re-runs. Do not bypass the guard; only
  `textbook_review_release_manual` may set `yggdrasill.manual_override`.
- Machines open findings with proposals; only an owner action changes data.
  Never auto-apply a proposal.
- Owner decisions send the fingerprint the screen showed. A proposal whose base
  changed is refused even after reload; the owner uses a manual edit instead.
- Decisions are append-only. Never update or delete `textbook_review_decisions`.
- Never change the source PDF. Record source errors as correction notes.
- Student code must not read review tables or functions.
- Outside the review screens (PDF export, answer/solution cards, problem-bank
  search, stats, assignment) read confirmed values from `pb_question_solutions`
  and `pb_question_meta`, never from `textbook_problem_analyses`. Only the
  subunit confirm (`textbook_review_apply_staged`) writes those two tables.
- The printed solution (`solution_transcribed`, `solution_source`) comes from
  Vision on the solution PDF crop or from the owner. Never fill it from the AI
  solve (`ai_solution`); keep the two apart. Strip `[해설]` / `[풀이]` headers
  and `16 답 ×` / `[정답]` answer lines from `solution_transcribed`
  (`cleanSolutionTranscribedText` / `textbook_review_clean_solution_text`) so
  the answer and `[해설]` label are never duplicated on V2 cards.
- Two-round review flow:
  1. **Round 1 ("중단원 문항 검수 실행")**:
     - Clean math problems (without missing/image answers) and clean
       non-figure quality problems that pass the original-compared V2 render
       check are **auto-approved (`approved`)** right away.
     - Pure rendering engine issues (`issue_kind = 'engine'`) are
       **auto-held (`held`)** and excluded from the error count and approval
       denominator.
     - Every problem with figures (`hasFigures`) is treated as a quality issue
       (`issue_kind = 'figure'`) so it goes through original comparison,
       automatic figure sizing/placement, and proposal presentation.
     - Every remaining math or quality error problem runs
       `textbook_problem_fix` (reading the body PDF original, set header PDF,
       and answer/solution PDF crop) to generate and present unified proposals
       (`fix_proposal.proposed_answer`, `stem`, `common_stem`, `choices`,
       `figure_layout`, `figure_crops`) in the UI editors without applying
       them to `pb_questions` / `textbook_problem_answers` yet.
  2. **Round 2 ("수학 일괄 처리" / "품질 일괄 처리")**:
     - After the owner reviews/tweaks the presented proposals, clicking
       "수학 일괄 처리" or "품질 일괄 처리" applies the proposals to DB
       (`textbook_problem_answers` + `pb_questions`), re-verifies only the
       affected problems, and approves those that pass.
- AI quality judgement is made from the V2 render images (what students see),
  not from the stem text. The manager app prepares the images (solution crop,
  V2 cards, and the original problem / set header rendered from the body PDF
  by `raw_page` + `item_region_1k`) and sends URLs/base64; the Edge Function
  does not call the gateway. Crop PNGs (`storage_key`) do not exist; never
  sign or read them.
- Figure size and position are computed in code from what the model measures
  on the original (figure box, text sample height and line count, placement);
  the model never writes `widthEm` or `figure_layout` itself. The em size
  uses the V2 line pitch (`LINE_PITCH_EM = 1.7` in `textbook_problem_fix.ts`);
  keep the size-ratio tolerance (0.8 to 1.25) the same in
  `textbook_problem_review.ts` (`FIGURE_SIZE_RATIO_*`) and the manager service
  (`kFigureSizeRatio*`).
- The 문항검수 right-hand stack renders with V2 only. Do not add the client
  LaTeX renderer there.
- `isReviewTodo` must stay identical in the Edge Function and the manager
  service; a failed Vision read is not retried automatically.
- The AI classifies quality issues (`issue_kind`: data/engine/figure) and may
  store a `fix_proposal`; it never writes `pb_questions`. Applying a stem,
  choices, common-stem or figure fix, or syncing the problem-bank answers,
  happens only through `textbook_review_apply_problem_fix` /
  `textbook_review_save_item_edit` on an owner action (the single
  "품질 검수 승인" button or "품질 일괄 처리", which approves only problems
  that pass the original-compared render check).
- Re-checking an approved problem against the original keeps `approved`; a
  difference only sets `render_checks.flagged_after_approval`.
- Stage 2 with `math_only` re-solves math `issue` problems (used by
  "수학 일괄 처리" after stem fixes) and writes only the math side. It must not
  touch quality checks, `quality_status`, `fix_proposal`, render checks or
  `solved_at`.
- `quality_status = 'held'` means a render-engine hold. Stage re-runs and
  render checks must keep `held` and `approved`; only an owner action
  (release or approval) changes them. Counts treat held problems separately
  from the approval target.
- `textbook_review_unit_overview` and similar builders: at most 50 pairs per
  `jsonb_build_object` call (Postgres 100-argument limit); split with `||`.
- In plpgsql, append to a `text[]` with `array_append(arr, 'x'::text)`, not
  `arr || 'x'` (the literal is read as an array literal: 22P02).
